ng","ingredient/lontong"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Peanut sauce","ingredient/peanut-sauce"],["Rice cake","ingredient/rice-cake"],["Rice vermicelli","ingredient/rice-vermicelli"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2e/Ketoprak_Boplo.JPG/500px-Ketoprak_Boplo.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Midori","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ketoprak_Boplo.JPG"}},"dish/lahoh":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/lahoh","n":"Lahoh","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Israeli cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Lahoh is a spongy, flat pancake-like bread. It is a type of flatbread eaten regularly in Somaliland, Somalia, Djibouti, Kenya, Ethiopia, Yemen and Saudi Arabia. Yemenite Jewish immigrants popularized the dish in Israel. It is also called canjeero/canjeelo in Somalia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-lahoh"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lahoh"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Self-rising flour","ingredient/self-rising-flour"],["Sorghum flour","ingredient/sorghum-flour"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]},{"h":"More from Israeli cuisine","links":[["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Hummus","dish/hummus"],["Sabich","dish/sabich"],["Sufganiyah","dish/sufganiyah"],["Taboon bread","dish/taboon-bread"],["Ziva (dish)","dish/ziva-dish"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/44/LahohS.jpg/500px-LahohS.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Gilabrand at English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LahohS.jpg"}},"ingredient/sakurab":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sakurab","n":"Sakurab","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Sakurab ( Allium chinense G. Don) is either a relative of the scallion (Allium fistulosum L.) or a white variant of the wild leek (Allium ampeloprasum). There have been journals discussing its growth patterns and potential usage as an ingredient in a healthy beverage with evidence to support either view.  It is a traditional food seasoning in the Philippines, used in the traditional cuisines in the islands of Mindanao and the Visayas where it is commonly known as sibujing."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sakurab"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakurab"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Palapa (condiment)","dish/palapa-condiment"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/11/Sakurab.jpg/500px-Sakurab.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Iskaid","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sakurab.jpg"}},"ingredient/sodium-alginate":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sodium-alginate","n":"Sodium alginate","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Alginic acid, also called algin, is a naturally occurring, edible polysaccharide found in brown algae.  It is hydrophilic and forms a viscous gum when hydrated. When the alginic acid binds with sodium and calcium ions, the resulting salts are known as alginates. Its colour ranges from white to yellowish-brown. It is sold in filamentous, granular, and powdered forms."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sodium-alginate"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_alginate"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Stracciatella (ice cream)","dish/stracciatella-ice-cream"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chocolate","ingredient/chocolate"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Gelatin","ingredient/gelatin"],["Ice cream","ingredient/ice-cream"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Milk chocolate","ingredient/milk-chocolate"],["Smetana","ingredient/smetana"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"ingredient/crushed-red-pepper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/crushed-red-pepper","n":"Crushed red pepper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Crushed red pepper or red pepper flakes or chilli flakes is a condiment or spice consisting of dried and crushed (as opposed to ground) red chilli peppers. This condiment is most often produced from cayenne-type peppers, although commercial producers may use a variety of different cultivars, usually within the 30,000–50,000 Scoville unit range. Often there is a high ratio of seeds, which are often erroneously believed to contain the most heat. Crushed red pepper is used by food manufacturers in pickling blends, chowders, spaghetti sauce, pizza sauce, soups and sausage."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-crushed-red-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crushed_red_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine",[["Vodka sauce","dish/vodka-sauce"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Pancetta","ingredient/pancetta"],["Penne","ingredient/penne"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Vodka","ingredient/vodka"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/32/2014_Dried_chilli_flakes.jpg/500px-2014_Dried_chilli_flakes.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Takeaway","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2014_Dried_chilli_flakes.jpg"}},"dish/zucchini-slice":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/zucchini-slice","n":"Zucchini slice","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#55b8ad","intro":[["Zucchini slice is a dish common in Australia and New Zealand that bears similarities to frittatas and quick breads. It consists of zucchini, eggs, cheese, usually bacon, and flour, baked to form a flat loaf. It is then cut into squares and served as a main dish or a side dish, often eaten for lunch."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-zucchini-slice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini_slice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Australian cuisine","cuisine/australian-cuisine"],["New Zealand cuisine","cuisine/new-zealand-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Zucchini","ingredient/zucchini"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Belly Rumbles: Australian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"bellyrumbles.com","note":"Sara McCleary's collection of Australian classics such as Anzac biscuits, pavlova, sausage rolls and native-ingredient bakes.","url":"https://bellyrumbles.com/category/australian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Eats","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipetineats.com","note":"Sydney-based Nagi Maehashi's widely used recipe site; broad in scope, but a staple of Australian home cooking.","url":"https://www.recipetineats.com/home/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Cloudy Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cloudykitchen.com","note":"New Zealand-born baker Erin Clarkson's blog, with a section of Kiwi classics.","url":"https://cloudykitchen.com/blog/category/new-zealand-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Australian cuisine","links":[["Anzac biscuit","dish/anzac-biscuit"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Flake (fish)","dish/flake-fish"],["Kangaroo meat","dish/kangaroo-meat"],["Parrot pie","dish/parrot-pie"],["Pavlova","dish/pavlova"],["Sausage sizzle","dish/sausage-sizzle"],["Steak and eggs","dish/steak-and-eggs"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/16/Zucchini_Slice_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Zucchini_Slice_%28cropped%29.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Valereee","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zucchini_Slice_(cropped).jpg"}}}